 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="1920" height="1080" alt="Rollable ribbon fiber optic cable" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></div><div class="section-introduction xpfskxn"><h2 class="xhz5zt5">What an enterprise network uses</h2><p class="xuvmvsv">An enterprise network runs on three kinds of fiber. Riser and plenum rated cable carries the backbone up and across the building. Trunks, cassettes and patch cords connect the server room or data hall. Outdoor cable links buildings on a campus. The rating follows the pathway, and the inspecting authority has the final say, so it belongs on the order rather than being assumed.</p></div><div class="specification-table xcqzusx fb"><div class="construction-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">In-building backbone</p><p class="xcclquv">Mini cable 8F and 12F at 3.0mm OD in OFNP, and indoor rollable ribbon 12F to 864F in plenum and riser ratings</p></div><div class="construction-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Ratings</p><p class="xcclquv">OFNP plenum, OFNR riser and LSZH</p></div><div class="construction-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Server room</p><p class="xcclquv">MTP and MPO trunks 12F to 864F, harness breakouts, cassettes and 1U panels at 144F per 1U</p></div><div class="construction-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Patching</p><p class="xcclquv">LC, SC, FC, ST and MTRJ patch cords, plus armored patch cords</p></div><div class="construction-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Fiber type</p><p class="xcclquv">OS2 single-mode for distance, OM3 and OM4 multimode for short reach</p></div><div class="construction-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Between buildings</p><p class="xcclquv">Outdoor loose tube cable (GCYFTY and GYFS), and armored direct burial cable for trenched routes</p></div><div class="standards-row xr2tetp"><p class="xbslay4">Lead time</p><p class="xcclquv">6 to 8 weeks from PO, 2 to 3 weeks by air, up to 10 weeks for custom builds</p></div></div></section><section class="fibre-count-range xqjs4fo"><h2 class="xqmzbdo">From the desk to the backbone</h2><p class="xbt6gdt">Low counts for in-building runs, high counts where pathway space is the constraint. Specified per route and supplied to order.</p><div class="count-rail xhrktuh"><div class="xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">1F</p></div><div class="xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">8F</p></div><div class="xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">12F</p></div><div class="xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">24F</p></div><div class="xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">144F</p></div><div class="xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">432F</p></div><div class="xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">864F</p></div></div></section><div class="section-divider xbstc8l"><div class="x2h0iev"></div><div class="xqo6eaw"></div><div class="x2h0iev"></div></div><div class="individual-products xjpxpkl"><h3 class="xntyyys">Enterprise cable and connectivity products</h3><div class="product-links xawjyfv">{["mini-cable-plenum", "rollable-ribbon-indoor", "armored-indoor-drop", "mpo-and-mtp-trunk", "lc-fiber-patch-cord", "armored-fiber-patch-cord", "loose-tube-stranded-dielectric", "armored-direct-burial"].map((id) => products.find((item) => item.id === id)).filter(Boolean).map((item) => (<ProductCard item={item} />))}</div></div><div class="section-divider xbstc8l"><div class="x2h0iev"></div><div class="xqo6eaw"></div><div class="x2h0iev"></div></div><section class="why-source-through-vocom x6mc4fb"><div class="why-introduction xn9jb0l"><h2 class="x2aydey">Why source it through Vocom</h2></div><div class="sourcing-reason-grid xyelmuz"><div class="build-to-order xwbyhvi fb"><svg class="xmhveue icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M 0 2.25 C 0 1.007 1.007 0 2.25 0 C 3.493 0 4.5 1.007 4.5 2.25 C 4.5 3.493 3.493 4.5 2.25 4.5 C 1.007 4.5 0 3.493 0 2.25 Z" fill-opacity="var(--icon-alpha, 0)" fill="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(7.5 5.25)"></path><path d="M 0 2.25 C 0 1.007 1.007 0 